{"causes": ["The post-World War II cultural climate fostered a spirit of experimentation in the arts, paving the way for the fusion of jazz with other genres.", "The rise of electric instruments in the 1960s allowed jazz musicians to explore new sounds and styles, merging jazz with rock and funk.", "The civil rights movement and the counterculture of the 1960s encouraged artists to break free from traditional constraints, resulting in innovative musical expressions."], "effects": ["Jazz fusion expanded the audience for jazz, attracting listeners from rock and pop backgrounds, which increased its popularity.", "The genre influenced countless musicians and led to the emergence of hybrid styles, including smooth jazz and progressive rock.", "Jazz fusion's experimental spirit contributed to the development of electronic music and new genres in the late 20th century."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "jazz-fusion", "sourceName": "Jazz Fusion", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "bitches-brew", "targetName": "Bitches Brew", "context": "The 1970 album 'Bitches Brew' by Miles Davis was a groundbreaking work that exemplified the principles of jazz fusion."}, {"sourceSlug": "jazz-fusion", "sourceName": "Jazz Fusion", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "smooth-jazz", "targetName": "Smooth Jazz", "context": "The rise of jazz fusion in the 1970s led directly to the development of smooth jazz as a more commercially viable genre."}, {"sourceSlug": "bitches-brew", "sourceName": "Bitches Brew", "verb": "TRANSFORMS", "targetSlug": "jazz-fusion", "targetName": "Jazz Fusion", "context": "'Bitches Brew' transformed the sound of jazz, integrating rock elements that would define jazz fusion for decades."}, {"sourceSlug": "jazz-fusion", "sourceName": "Jazz Fusion", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "return-to-forever", "targetName": "Return to Forever", "context": "The genre's popularity helped create bands like Return to Forever, which became integral to the jazz fusion movement."}, {"sour